# Special route

Add a special route only when a verified task cannot be served by an existing dashboard, setting or guide, and record who owns it. Keep the native route working if the custom one fails. The shared limits for every page template are on [Page templates](index.html).

## When to use it

In Civica this means a deliberately scoped custom component or a documented native route. Record its owner, route and compatibility boundary ([WG-090](../../content/publish-update-retire/choose-content-type.html#wg-090)). [Compatibility register and native fallback](../../home-assistant/compatibility-register.html) owns which native surfaces Civica claims to support.

## Structure and behaviour

Keep the same headings, navigation, focus and status conventions as the rest of Civica. Specify the input data, the allowed actions and the empty and error states. Native navigation must keep supporting browser history and ordinary links. Give a recovery that matches the cause when the source fails ([WG-040](../../content/writing-guidelines/states-and-errors.html#wg-040)).

## Home Assistant boundary

A theme is not permission to take over arbitrary Home Assistant routes or private components. A new page must not invent backend services or expose private household data. The examples show route information and a recovery state. They are not an installed custom panel.

